# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded power x^y of B16
#
# x^y = e^(y ln(x)), with ln from a 64-entry table and a polynomial and e^t
# from a 64-entry table and a polynomial, all in B64, then rounded once to
# B16. Exact powers of two are built directly. For y in a small set of
# multiples of 1/4 a result that may be exact is rounded to its nearby B64
# value with 24 bits when an exact square-and-multiply check agrees. A few
# inputs the approximation rounds wrongly are listed. Round to nearest only,
# with the C pow special cases: overflow gives ±inf, a negative base with a
# non-integer exponent gives NaN, x^±0 = 1 and 1^y = 1 (except for a
# signaling NaN), (-1)^±inf = 1, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/pow/powf16.c via RazorForge's B16Pow.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Maxence Ponsardin
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/Core

